<title>GERMANY: VW cancels two shifts over Spain strike.</title>
<headline>VW cancels two shifts over Spain strike.</headline>
<dateline>WOLFSBURG, Germany 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>German carmaker Volkswagen said on Wednesday that it was cancelling two special shifts at its Wolfsburg plant over the next week as the fall-out from the Sapanish truckers' strike continues.</p>
<p>VW said the early shift on February 22 and night shift on February 24 to produce its Golf and Polo models had been cancelled as the necessary supplies had not come through.</p>
<p>In a note to employees made available on Wednesday, VW said the shifts would be compensated for in special shifts on March 22 and March 24.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
